#NEXUS
[ Dieudonné, Paulina-Carabajal & Cruzado-Caballero 2026/2027, Cretaceous Research 189: 106478,
  doi:10.1016/j.cretres.2026.106478, Fig. 13 (p. 31): reduced strict consensus tree of ornithopods,
  time-scaled. Topology transcribed from the figure image (vision model, then checked by eye against
  an enlarged figure and against the 107 taxon names of the paper's matrix, supplement mmc4).
  Internal node labels = printed support, 'Bremer/bootstrap' (bootstrap shown only when >50%);
  'DRYOSAURIDAE' and 'DYSALOTOSAURINAE' added at the nodes of the figure's coloured boxes.
  Branch lengths/time scaling NOT transcribed. Taxon names use the MATRIX spellings; the figure prints
  four of them differently: Cumnoria prestwichi, Uteodon aphanooecetes, Fostoria dhinbangunmal, Rhabdodon sp.1.
  Support values are small in the source image: confirm against the figure before quoting. ]

